part_seam() {
  heading $1
  say "seam is the engine under the symbol view, and it has a view of its own: a page with the change as a graph, one box a definition and an arrow a mention. A solid arrow is a mention in a signature, so a change carries outward along it; a dashed one is in a body, where it stops."
  say "${k}g${r} on the page switches to the reading order: the same change as numbered threads, and ${k}space${r} marks one definition read and moves on. The page is one self-contained file, so it can be sent to someone."
  say "In the symbol view or a review, ${k}G${r} opens it on the row you are on, and in gmr's list on the MR."
  local kw=20
  key "seam <range> --html" "the page"
  key "seam <range> --score" "the shape, as s showed it"
  key "seam --mr 1234" "any GitLab MR, through glab"
  ask "Open this change's page in your browser?" || return
  demo_reset
  (cd $repo && seam origin/main...HEAD --html)
  pause
}

part_staging() {
  heading $1
  demo_reset
  cat > $repo/src/fees.ts <<'EOF'
import type { Order } from "./order";

export const RESTOCKING_WINDOW_DAYS = 30;
const FEE_RATE = 0;

export function daysSince(from: Date, to: Date): number {
  return Math.floor((to.getTime() - from.getTime()) / 86_400_000);
}

// Returns inside the window are free; after it, a share of the total.
export function restockingFee(order: Order, returnedAt: Date): number {
  if (feeWaived(order)) return 0;
  if (daysSince(order.deliveredAt, returnedAt) <= RESTOCKING_WINDOW_DAYS) return 0;
  return Math.round(order.total * FEE_RATE * 100) / 100;
}

// Orders over $500 never pay a restocking fee.
export function feeWaived(order: Order): boolean {
  return order.total > 500;
}
EOF
  say "The symbol view works on your own uncommitted work too: it is what ga opens. The demo now has two changes in one file, src/fees.ts: a new feeWaived rule with restockingFee calling it, which you want to commit, and FEE_RATE set to 0 while you were testing, which you do not."
  look 1 "Each row has the stage cells ga's file rows have: staged, then unstaged."
  look 2 "${k}space${r} on feeWaived stages that function alone, then restockingFee. The file's diff is cut to the symbol's lines, so FEE_RATE stays unstaged in the same file."
  look 3 "${k}c${r} commits what is staged, in your editor with the diff below. ${k}f${r} is the file panel, where ${k}p${r} stages by hunk and ${k}d${r} discards."
  say "Hunk staging gets you there too, when the hunks happen to fall apart. By symbol, the unit is the thing you meant to change."
  launch ga
  demo_reset
}

